00:37:31.591 --> 00:37:33.439
If you want, I can talk to him.


00:37:34.831 --> 00:37:35.831
Oh!


00:37:38.288 --> 00:37:40.247
Just have fun tonight.


00:37:41.124 --> 00:37:43.255
He misses you.


00:37:43.339 --> 00:37:44.713
Hi, Harry.


00:37:45.174 --> 00:37:46.728
Good to see you.


00:37:47.469 --> 00:37:49.203
Sorry I'm late, honey.


00:37:50.907 --> 00:37:52.933
Have you had anything to eat?


00:37:53.017 --> 00:37:55.679
No, I'll...
I'll grab something later.


00:37:55.704 --> 00:37:57.822
No, no, but I've got vouchers.


00:37:57.879 --> 00:37:59.353
- Yeah?
- Yup.


00:37:59.570 --> 00:38:02.186
Hotdog or hotdog?


00:38:02.266 --> 00:38:04.128
Well, hotdog then.


00:38:04.870 --> 00:38:06.244
Harry?


00:38:06.328 --> 00:38:09.248
I'll get something to eat with Oleg.


00:38:19.378 --> 00:38:21.144
So, how are things with you?


00:38:22.479 --> 00:38:24.704
- All right.
- Yeah?


00:38:24.792 --> 00:38:26.266
A bit tired.


00:38:26.303 --> 00:38:28.636
You've been working too hard,
haven't you?


00:38:30.460 --> 00:38:32.621
I can't sleep.


00:38:34.036 --> 00:38:36.083
You should try Valcetet.


00:38:37.373 --> 00:38:39.022
It's a new one.


00:38:40.054 --> 00:38:41.578
It'll help you sleep.


00:38:42.589 --> 00:38:45.261
I can give you
a prescription right now.


00:38:45.736 --> 00:38:47.257
- Really?
- Yeah.


00:38:47.315 --> 00:38:49.616
- With that?
- Yeah.


00:39:02.208 --> 00:39:05.273
She won't allow me
to try and find my father.


00:39:05.308 --> 00:39:07.704
Your mother
should be the judge of that.


00:39:10.978 --> 00:39:12.823
She won't listen to me.


00:39:13.087 --> 00:39:14.806
She's worried about you.


00:39:16.474 --> 00:39:18.779
All she cares about is herself.


00:39:18.804 --> 00:39:20.328
All she cares about is you.


00:39:20.351 --> 00:39:23.280
That's why she dumped me.


00:39:23.305 --> 00:39:25.105
I'm such a bad influence.


00:39:25.207 --> 00:39:27.212
She's concerned.


00:39:27.959 --> 00:39:29.898
Concerned about what?


00:39:30.703 --> 00:39:33.073
The fact that
you'll run away from home.


00:39:34.248 --> 00:39:36.034
The fact that
you've been drinking.


00:39:37.459 --> 00:39:40.021
So, you're
gonna give me a lecture


00:39:40.046 --> 00:39:41.713
about drinking?


00:39:43.729 --> 00:39:45.219
Don't be a prick.


00:39:46.208 --> 00:39:48.104
Your mom told me
the school's arranged


00:39:48.129 --> 00:39:50.198
a father and son
camping trip.


00:39:50.539 --> 00:39:52.442
If you want, I can come.


00:39:53.147 --> 00:39:56.242
But you're not her
boyfriend anymore.


00:39:57.449 --> 00:39:58.893
So?


00:40:03.056 --> 00:40:05.630
Yeah. Yeah.


00:40:06.228 --> 00:40:07.997
I want you to come.


00:40:09.675 --> 00:40:11.926
- You sure?
- Yeah.


00:40:13.096 --> 00:40:14.514
Good.


00:40:14.650 --> 00:40:18.278
So, what's the... the big surprise?


00:40:19.376 --> 00:40:20.827
Eh...


00:40:21.608 --> 00:40:23.651
Let's find out.


00:40:24.084 --> 00:40:26.561
Someone at work
got me the tickets.


00:40:37.546 --> 00:40:39.394
You've got a message.


00:40:39.904 --> 00:40:41.820
Let me see what it says.


00:40:44.293 --> 00:40:46.059
I've gotta make a call.


00:40:46.144 --> 00:40:47.717
Will you stay here?


00:40:49.853 --> 00:40:52.642
<i>Harry, there's another missing woman.
In Geilo, this time.</i>


00:40:52.809 --> 00:40:54.450
That's not our jurisdiction.


00:40:54.530 --> 00:40:56.126
<i>I think we should
have a look at this.</i>


00:40:56.151 --> 00:40:58.577
<i>I'm gonna be with you
in two minutes, okay?</i>


00:40:58.634 --> 00:41:01.069
<i>Her husband specifically
asked for you.</i>


00:41:08.419 --> 00:41:09.927
Hello.


00:41:10.063 --> 00:41:10.880
- Hi.
- Oh.


00:41:10.905 --> 00:41:12.876
I didn't expect you so early.


00:41:12.918 --> 00:41:14.505
- Something came up.
- Oh.


00:41:14.552 --> 00:41:16.092
Hi, Harry.


00:41:16.176 --> 00:41:18.088
How was the concert?


00:41:19.886 --> 00:41:21.825
Yeah, it was-it was great.


00:41:24.576 --> 00:41:26.139
We spoke.


00:41:27.044 --> 00:41:30.878
I'm taking him on the
father and son camping trip...


00:41:31.781 --> 00:41:33.232
thing.


00:41:36.546 --> 00:41:37.703
See you.


00:41:37.728 --> 00:41:38.847
Hey.


00:41:39.097 --> 00:41:40.205
Bye.


00:41:44.923 --> 00:41:47.979
Take me home.
We'll go in the morning.


00:42:29.736 --> 00:42:31.582
Who reported her missing?


00:42:31.607 --> 00:42:34.688
Her husband, last night. 20:05.


00:42:35.652 --> 00:42:38.802
Sylvia Ottersen, 33 years old.


00:42:39.262 --> 00:42:40.849
Self-employed.


00:42:41.348 --> 00:42:42.901
Married twice.


00:42:43.174 --> 00:42:44.716
But no children.


00:43:02.377 --> 00:43:03.772
Hello?


00:43:06.048 --> 00:43:07.263
Hello?


00:43:10.118 --> 00:43:11.376
Hello?


00:43:44.618 --> 00:43:45.763
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:43:46.720 --> 00:43:48.110
Can I help you?


00:43:48.701 --> 00:43:51.422
Yeah, well, we're with the
Oslo police.


00:43:52.829 --> 00:43:55.437
We got the missing persons call.


00:43:55.751 --> 00:43:58.087
Oh. Who's missing?


00:43:58.984 --> 00:44:01.068
Sylvia Ottersen.


00:44:01.093 --> 00:44:02.972
I'm Sylvia Ottersen.


00:44:03.758 --> 00:44:05.763
What? You're Sylvia Ottersen?


00:44:05.823 --> 00:44:09.047
Why... why would your husband
report you missing?


00:44:09.443 --> 00:44:10.767
I have no idea.


00:44:10.792 --> 00:44:13.009
He's not the kind to
play practical jokes.


00:44:13.400 --> 00:44:15.736
- Is he here?
- No.


00:44:16.069 --> 00:44:18.165
He's gone to the station
to pick up my sister.


00:44:18.503 --> 00:44:19.785
Okay.


00:44:19.856 --> 00:44:22.391
Well, I guess
it must be a crank call.


00:44:22.658 --> 00:44:25.642
We didn't know where you were,
so we had a look inside the house.


00:44:26.652 --> 00:44:29.715
I turned your music off.
Sorry about that.


00:44:31.273 --> 00:44:33.149
Thank you.


00:44:38.056 --> 00:44:39.664
Can I just ask you...


00:44:39.910 --> 00:44:42.699
Is it just you and your husband?
Or do you have any children?


00:44:44.360 --> 00:44:45.963
No, it's just us.


00:44:47.860 --> 00:44:50.484
Okay, thank you.


00:45:05.419 --> 00:45:07.233
God, what do you think
you're doing?


00:45:07.598 --> 00:45:09.886
You know damn well
what I'm talking about.


00:45:11.188 --> 00:45:13.263
Calling the police,
telling them I'm missing?


00:45:14.237 --> 00:45:16.027
You think that's funny?


00:45:16.109 --> 00:45:18.261
Don't you understand?
It's over.


00:45:18.611 --> 00:45:20.458
I don't want to see you again.


00:45:21.528 --> 00:45:25.028
No, it wasn't your child.
It was mine.


00:45:25.736 --> 00:45:28.591
If you call one more time,
I'm going to the police.


00:46:42.484 --> 00:46:46.529
<i>HQ to DC Bratt... DC Bratt?</i>


00:46:46.554 --> 00:46:48.176
Yeah, speaking.


00:46:48.236 --> 00:46:52.292
<i>We've had a missing persons report.
A woman named Sylvia Ottersen.</i>


00:46:52.385 --> 00:46:55.070
Oh, no, she's fine.
W-we just left her.


00:46:55.742 --> 00:46:58.575
<i>Well, the call came in
two minutes ago.</i>


00:46:59.152 --> 00:47:02.303
<i>Her husband asked specifically
for Inspector Hole.</i>


00:47:02.385 --> 00:47:04.230
How could...


00:47:05.013 --> 00:47:06.552
Turn the car around.


00:47:23.642 --> 00:47:25.150
Sylvia?


00:47:27.662 --> 00:47:29.814
Sorry we're back, Mrs. Ottersen.


00:47:29.984 --> 00:47:32.092
We just wanted to make sure
you were all right.


00:47:32.364 --> 00:47:34.357
I'm Ane Pedersen.


00:47:35.298 --> 00:47:38.425
Sylvia's my sister.
We're twins.


00:47:38.450 --> 00:47:39.866
Who are you?


00:49:16.380 --> 00:49:19.352
- Is that enough?
- Yeah, keep going.


00:49:19.475 --> 00:49:21.241
Did you find Hagen?


00:49:21.266 --> 00:49:23.318
He's at the dinner
at City Hall.


00:49:24.132 --> 00:49:26.298
Keep it clear, if you can.


00:49:47.149 --> 00:49:49.040
Well, she always liked men.


00:49:50.185 --> 00:49:52.362
Ever since we were teenagers.


00:49:55.267 --> 00:49:56.965
She was a good person.


00:49:58.394 --> 00:50:00.333
She didn't want to hurt anyone.


00:50:01.284 --> 00:50:03.186
It's just the way she was.


00:50:08.726 --> 00:50:11.463
I know your sister
didn't have any children.


00:50:12.757 --> 00:50:15.645
It was just that there was something
in her reaction that when I asked...


00:50:15.679 --> 00:50:17.278
She was pregnant.


00:50:20.964 --> 00:50:24.092
She wasn't sure
who the father was.


00:50:27.240 --> 00:50:29.894
She got rid of the baby
a few weeks ago.


00:51:17.534 --> 00:51:20.820
Ladies and gentlemen,
introducing our guest of honor...


00:51:20.884 --> 00:51:23.423
King of industry, philanthropist...


00:51:23.606 --> 00:51:25.988
and head of Oslo's Winter Games bid...


00:51:26.072 --> 00:51:28.488
Arve Stop.


00:51:29.119 --> 00:51:31.165
So lovely for you
to be here for us.


00:51:31.258 --> 00:51:32.303
I'm not on the list, but
I know many of these


00:51:32.328 --> 00:51:34.161
people are supposed
to be on the list.


00:51:34.186 --> 00:51:37.435
I'm the most old friend
of Arve Stop's, you see.


00:51:37.488 --> 00:51:39.512
There's been some
kind of misunderstanding.


00:51:39.538 --> 00:51:42.453
- I have a person named Vetlesen.
- Come right up, yeah you can come in.


00:51:42.506 --> 00:51:44.450
He says he's
a friend of Arve Stop.


00:51:45.459 --> 00:51:46.623
No, wait, wait.


00:51:46.648 --> 00:51:49.109
No, it's fine, No, just relax.
Just relax.


00:51:51.724 --> 00:51:53.848
I wonder, with a dozen companies...


00:51:54.311 --> 00:51:55.556
when people ask me why...


00:51:55.612 --> 00:51:59.096
I've given up so much
of my time to lead this bid.


00:51:59.180 --> 00:52:02.827
I tell them, it's because
I never had these opportunities.


00:52:02.888 --> 00:52:07.311
When I was a boy, the only
winter sports I engaged in were...


00:52:07.668 --> 00:52:11.556
the uphill snow shovel
and the 50-meter firewood carry.


00:52:15.596 --> 00:52:18.987
That is why I believe
passionately...


00:52:19.080 --> 00:52:21.667
that this Cup is about
much more than just


00:52:21.692 --> 00:52:23.956
publicity for our fair city.


00:52:33.724 --> 00:52:34.972
Homicides?


00:52:35.056 --> 00:52:38.636
Just missing persons for now.
But the pattern is disturbing.


00:52:38.903 --> 00:52:42.189
And... I received this.


00:52:46.808 --> 00:52:48.004
Prints?


00:52:49.696 --> 00:52:50.912
It isn't just the letter.


00:52:50.972 --> 00:52:53.603
He reported her missing
before he killed her.


00:52:53.634 --> 00:52:55.798
He was watching us
the entire time.


00:52:58.640 --> 00:53:01.425
- What do you need?
- Small team.


00:53:01.632 --> 00:53:03.724
I'll set up a separate
incident room at the mill.


00:53:03.808 --> 00:53:06.500
All right. I don't want a word
of this to be leaked to the...


00:53:06.540 --> 00:53:08.575
- To the press.
- the press, yeah.


00:53:08.647 --> 00:53:10.519
Not until this fucking bid is over.


00:53:42.250 --> 00:53:44.856
Try to... Just... try to smile.


00:53:45.972 --> 00:53:48.234
Smile, it's good.


00:53:50.184 --> 00:53:53.221
Does this strike you as the
proper time and place for this?


00:53:56.016 --> 00:53:57.764
Wait.


00:54:21.750 --> 00:54:23.523
Idiot.


00:54:23.588 --> 00:54:25.710
What? Arve?


00:54:26.277 --> 00:54:30.646
What? No, don't cry.
Listen, why...


00:54:38.382 --> 00:54:39.679
Shit.


00:54:59.096 --> 00:55:00.242
Hey.


00:55:01.636 --> 00:55:02.800
Hey!


00:55:09.313 --> 00:55:10.477
Get out.


00:55:11.839 --> 00:55:12.981
Get out!


00:55:29.793 --> 00:55:31.050
Hey!


00:55:32.875 --> 00:55:34.515
Oi! Hey!


00:55:35.258 --> 00:55:41.078
Annette Elden, 33, disappeared
12th of December, 2006.


00:55:41.487 --> 00:55:43.804
Her head washed
ashore near Arendal.


00:55:43.829 --> 00:55:45.733
The rest of the body
never found.


00:55:45.956 --> 00:55:49.615
Forensic report indicates
saw marks on her neck.


00:55:50.221 --> 00:55:55.767
Status: Unmarried.
Two children by different fathers.


00:55:55.994 --> 00:55:58.224
Harry, I've got the
names and the addresses


00:55:58.249 --> 00:55:59.642
of Sylvia Ottersen's boyfriends.


00:55:59.946 --> 00:56:02.269
Now, she went to the clinic
the 2nd of November...


00:56:02.335 --> 00:56:05.516
but they won't break
patient confidentiality.


00:56:06.079 --> 00:56:08.954
They do, however, perform abortions.


00:56:14.571 --> 00:56:16.031
What is it?


00:56:16.547 --> 00:56:19.111
- Magnus, get me the list.
- What list?


00:56:19.158 --> 00:56:21.370
The list of doctors at the Gellion.


00:56:21.454 --> 00:56:23.786
I'm thinking that he's going...


00:56:23.870 --> 00:56:25.898
- after women that he disapproves of.
- Here.


00:56:25.930 --> 00:56:28.700
All the doctors at Gellion
from the last five years.


00:56:29.826 --> 00:56:31.980
How did he know?


00:56:32.795 --> 00:56:35.049
How did he know
Sylvia Ottersen was pregnant?


00:56:41.536 --> 00:56:42.908
Idar Vetlesen.


00:56:44.338 --> 00:56:47.294
Birte Becker had an
appointment with the same doctor.


00:57:11.423 --> 00:57:12.989
Dr. Idar Vetlesen?


00:57:13.014 --> 00:57:14.987
Yes, that's me.


00:57:15.257 --> 00:57:16.673
Step in.


00:57:16.694 --> 00:57:19.694
Birte Becker and Sylvia Ottersen
were both patients of yours?


00:57:19.778 --> 00:57:22.852
Uh, no, they were both
patients at the clinic.


00:57:22.877 --> 00:57:25.218
Uh, I never met Sylvia Ottersen.


00:57:25.278 --> 00:57:26.886
Can you tell me who treated her?


00:57:27.084 --> 00:57:30.011
No, I'm bound
by patient confidentiality.


00:57:31.218 --> 00:57:32.554
She's dead.


00:57:32.777 --> 00:57:33.837
Oh.


00:57:34.750 --> 00:57:35.888
Oh, no.


00:57:36.549 --> 00:57:39.266
Wait...
well, doctor confidentiality.


00:57:39.286 --> 00:57:42.664
In theory, would it be possible for
you to access her medical files?


00:57:42.743 --> 00:57:44.265
Even if you didn't
treat her yourself?


00:57:44.290 --> 00:57:45.842
Well, in theory, yes.


00:57:46.314 --> 00:57:49.600
The doctors at the clinic have
access to the files of every patient...


00:57:49.640 --> 00:57:52.521
should they choose to
look at them, which I did not.


00:57:53.278 --> 00:57:55.412
What did you see Birte Becker about?


00:57:55.437 --> 00:57:57.956
Well, that is uh, confidential.


00:57:58.008 --> 00:57:59.769
How do you know Arve Stop?


00:58:01.130 --> 00:58:02.268
- Arve?
- Hmm.


00:58:02.818 --> 00:58:04.781
Well, I've known Arve for years.


00:58:06.738 --> 00:58:08.654
I do research on premature birth.


00:58:08.738 --> 00:58:10.672
We have a small charity, and...


00:58:10.697 --> 00:58:12.569
Arve Stop is one of
our biggest supporters.


00:58:12.594 --> 00:58:15.622
Huh, I wouldn't have thought a man
who goes on so much about family values


00:58:15.647 --> 00:58:18.292
would support a clinic
that specializes in abortion.


00:58:19.389 --> 00:58:21.920
Well, we specialize
in many different areas.


00:58:21.945 --> 00:58:22.768
Hmm.


00:58:22.793 --> 00:58:26.435
And Mr. Stop supports our
research in premature birth.


00:58:26.460 --> 00:58:28.356
So, do you see each other socially?


00:58:29.365 --> 00:58:31.849
Yeah, well, that depends
on how you mean.


00:58:31.889 --> 00:58:33.730
It's quite simple, actually.
Do you have friends in common?


00:58:33.928 --> 00:58:36.689
Yes, we-we mix in the same circles, so.


00:58:36.777 --> 00:58:38.147
W-why are you uh...


00:58:38.172 --> 00:58:39.047
To know if you were...


00:58:39.072 --> 00:58:41.742
Have you ever practiced in other
parts of the country, Dr. Vetlesen?


00:58:41.767 --> 00:58:45.347
Yes, I have in Eidsvoll,
in uh, Lillehammer.


00:58:45.372 --> 00:58:46.886
I see you have a picture of
Mon Plaisir pavilion...


00:58:46.946 --> 00:58:49.110
- in Bergen.
- Yes, yes, in Bergen.


00:58:50.775 --> 00:58:52.443
Do you live alone?


00:58:54.194 --> 00:58:56.818
Yes, I uh, I am a reluctant bachelor.


00:58:56.902 --> 00:58:58.963
Is there anyone
in the house right now?


00:59:00.998 --> 00:59:03.778
Because I thought I saw someone
in the window when I passed.


00:59:05.238 --> 00:59:09.610
Well, if you want to take a look around,
I will need to see a search warrant.


00:59:09.635 --> 00:59:12.220
In fact, if you don't mind,


00:59:12.245 --> 00:59:14.342
I would like to call my lawyer...


00:59:14.627 --> 00:59:16.902
before I answer any more
of your questions.


00:59:16.986 --> 00:59:19.111
That won't be necessary,
Dr. Vetlesen.


00:59:20.538 --> 00:59:22.824
You can bring your lawyer
when we see you next time.


00:59:28.326 --> 00:59:30.317
- Hey.
- Hi.


00:59:31.300 --> 00:59:32.468
What was that?


00:59:33.446 --> 00:59:36.070
- What?
- He isn't a suspect yet.


00:59:36.154 --> 00:59:38.401
We needed permission
to search the house.


00:59:38.566 --> 00:59:39.849
I know that.


00:59:40.312 --> 00:59:42.415
Why'd you ask him
about Arve Stop?


00:59:44.616 --> 00:59:46.746
I saw a picture
of them both together.


00:59:47.116 --> 00:59:48.293
And?


00:59:48.782 --> 00:59:50.570
And it was an innocent question.


00:59:50.654 --> 00:59:53.496
Jesus, anyone can see he's
trying to hide something, right?


01:00:11.938 --> 01:00:14.218
Cloudberry.


01:00:17.318 --> 01:00:19.457
If you hadn't told me
to look out for it,


01:00:19.482 --> 01:00:21.875
I'd have assumed she was
attached to his security detail.


01:00:21.902 --> 01:00:23.117
Cloudberry?


01:00:23.142 --> 01:00:25.050
It's her password.


01:00:27.546 --> 01:00:31.070
<i>Does this strike you as the
proper time and place for this?</i>


01:00:36.362 --> 01:00:38.074
Arve Stop.


01:00:38.099 --> 01:00:39.026
<i>Idiot.</i>


01:00:39.051 --> 01:00:42.026
She filmed him at rallies...


01:00:42.110 --> 01:00:45.278
at restaurants, at home.


01:01:04.694 --> 01:01:06.056
Hi.


01:01:07.490 --> 01:01:09.204
Do you want a ride?


01:01:11.232 --> 01:01:12.237
No.


01:01:22.392 --> 01:01:23.810
Bye.


01:02:21.179 --> 01:02:25.344
<i>The 8:45 train to Bergen
leaving on platform five.</i>


01:02:27.031 --> 01:02:28.261
Oh, sorry.


01:02:31.341 --> 01:02:33.960
<i>This is the 8:45
service to Bergen</i>


01:02:33.985 --> 01:02:37.310
<i>which stops in Gol,
Finse, Voss and Bergen.</i>


01:02:37.816 --> 01:02:40.631
<i>The next station is Gol.</i>


01:02:59.164 --> 01:03:00.579
Hi, Harry.


01:03:03.368 --> 01:03:04.439
Hi.


01:03:04.578 --> 01:03:06.416
Hiding in the playroom, are we?


01:03:06.443 --> 01:03:07.515
Yes.


01:03:09.049 --> 01:03:11.673
Don't worry,
I'm getting off at the next stop.


01:03:13.215 --> 01:03:14.539
Going far?


01:03:14.564 --> 01:03:15.679
Bergen.


01:03:15.786 --> 01:03:17.987
Ah, rather you than me.


01:03:18.251 --> 01:03:21.444
Then again, I'm attending
a three-day conference on


01:03:21.469 --> 01:03:23.991
bio-identical hormone restoration.


01:03:24.051 --> 01:03:26.352
I thought you were a plastic surgeon?


01:03:26.517 --> 01:03:27.667
Well, you know...


01:03:27.692 --> 01:03:31.050
Cosmetic surgery needs
to move with the times, too.


01:03:31.785 --> 01:03:34.967
We're swapping the scalpel
for hormone replacement therapy.


01:03:36.529 --> 01:03:38.651
If you can slow down
the aging process...


01:03:38.676 --> 01:03:40.743
there won't be any
need for face-lifts, will there?


01:03:41.342 --> 01:03:43.806
I'll bear that in mind.


01:03:46.251 --> 01:03:48.293
So, how's the prescription working?


01:03:49.801 --> 01:03:51.296
Sleeping like a baby.


01:03:51.785 --> 01:03:52.975
Splendid.


01:03:54.386 --> 01:03:58.308
So, you, you canceled the Oleg thing?


01:04:00.690 --> 01:04:02.444
The school trip?


01:04:02.543 --> 01:04:04.294
Weren't you supposed to...


01:04:04.439 --> 01:04:06.078
Oh, shit.


01:04:08.863 --> 01:04:10.658
- Shit!
- I'm sorry, Harry, uh...


01:04:10.683 --> 01:04:12.596
- I'm sure he's fine.
- Oleg, you coming?


01:04:12.616 --> 01:04:13.791
Come on.


01:04:13.816 --> 01:04:15.897
He knows how busy you are.


01:04:15.940 --> 01:04:17.188
Shit.


01:04:18.765 --> 01:04:21.593
Look, look, y-you're
not his father, Harry.


01:04:22.669 --> 01:04:24.178
What does that mean?


01:04:24.889 --> 01:04:25.795
Well, uh...


01:04:25.820 --> 01:04:27.755
I don't have to be
his father to care about him.


01:04:27.780 --> 01:04:29.159
I'm trying to say that...


01:04:29.184 --> 01:04:33.026
it's a big enough responsibility
for a real father, isn't it?


01:04:33.356 --> 01:04:35.205
Let alone you and me.


01:04:37.054 --> 01:04:38.244
I'm sorry, Harry.


01:04:38.269 --> 01:04:39.459
No.


01:04:45.393 --> 01:04:48.012
Did you hear from him?


01:04:48.037 --> 01:04:49.840
Why can't I go?


01:04:49.865 --> 01:04:51.131
Can I go with you?


01:04:51.156 --> 01:04:52.154
It's done!


01:04:55.365 --> 01:04:57.616
Hi, Oleg, it's Mathias.


01:04:58.185 --> 01:05:01.318
You know what, uh, I forgot to
check my messages last night, and...


01:05:01.342 --> 01:05:05.318
Harry called to say that
he couldn't make your trip.


01:05:06.028 --> 01:05:07.543
No, I know.


01:05:08.532 --> 01:05:12.444
No, h-he couldn't get through
to you or you mom, apparently.


01:05:13.237 --> 01:05:16.467
No, it's totally my fault, Oleg.


01:05:16.492 --> 01:05:18.364
Yes... yes... I'm sorry.


01:05:19.290 --> 01:05:20.735
Sorry, Oleg... yes...


01:05:22.497 --> 01:05:23.513
Yeah.


01:05:24.098 --> 01:05:28.613
So, I'll see you in a few days, then...
when I'm back from the conference.


01:05:32.559 --> 01:05:34.690
You didn't have to do that.


01:06:19.509 --> 01:06:21.596
Ready? That's it.


01:06:22.688 --> 01:06:25.360
Hey, Aasen, someone here
to speak to you.


01:06:30.690 --> 01:06:31.849
Aasen.


01:06:36.858 --> 01:06:39.580
My family owned
all of these buildings.


01:06:39.605 --> 01:06:41.096
And that house over there, too.


01:06:42.165 --> 01:06:44.038
Arve Stop worked for us back then.


01:06:44.059 --> 01:06:47.171
He was uh, bright, ambitious.


01:06:48.426 --> 01:06:50.701
My father really believed in him.


01:06:52.677 --> 01:06:55.908
The business wasn't going very well,
so we, uh, offered him a stake.


01:06:57.022 --> 01:06:59.839
And within a year,
he had forced us out.


01:06:59.864 --> 01:07:01.943
Sold the land for a fortune.


01:07:04.113 --> 01:07:07.866
Have any of my colleagues
been in touch with you recently?


01:07:08.387 --> 01:07:10.474
A young lady?


01:07:10.499 --> 01:07:11.490
No.


01:07:12.040 --> 01:07:17.799
I look at this picture now...
See Laila staring at him.


01:07:18.726 --> 01:07:20.769
I had no idea at the time.


01:07:22.726 --> 01:07:25.021
Family man, eh?


01:07:27.618 --> 01:07:30.871
Do you remember the name
of your wife's doctor?


01:07:31.193 --> 01:07:34.033
Sure. Morton Freiberg.


01:07:38.120 --> 01:07:41.746
Did she... ever see someone
called Vetlesen?


01:07:42.072 --> 01:07:44.485
Vetlesen? No.


01:07:44.510 --> 01:07:46.656
Dr. Idar Vetlesen.


01:07:50.262 --> 01:07:51.333
No.


01:07:52.893 --> 01:07:57.231
Any idea where I might find the
officer who's in charge of the case?


01:07:57.316 --> 01:08:02.519
Rafto? H-he died.


01:08:02.701 --> 01:08:06.891
Yeah, h-he died around
the same time.


01:08:51.913 --> 01:08:55.119
Detective Rafto.


01:08:55.144 --> 01:08:58.168
Can you connect me
to Haukeland hospital?


01:08:58.793 --> 01:09:00.778
What is this?
Am I under arrest?


01:09:01.451 --> 01:09:02.655
A cake?


01:09:02.676 --> 01:09:06.644
I need some information on a patient.
Laila Aasen.


01:09:07.120 --> 01:09:10.960
No, I don't-listen to me.
I don't know the admitting doctor.


01:09:11.044 --> 01:09:13.401
But perhaps she was there
for an abortion?


01:09:13.424 --> 01:09:15.279
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪


01:09:15.304 --> 01:09:19.835
Well, then, I'll come down there
with a fucking warrant myself.


01:09:20.556 --> 01:09:24.088
♪ Happy birthday,
dear Swensson ♪


01:09:24.113 --> 01:09:27.072
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪


01:09:27.097 --> 01:09:29.139
- Rafto?
- Idiot.


01:09:30.471 --> 01:09:33.042
Incompetent sons of...


01:09:34.455 --> 01:09:36.042
- Oi!
- Rafto?


01:09:37.202 --> 01:09:38.444
Rafto!


01:09:40.153 --> 01:09:42.112
What's he doing?


01:09:46.195 --> 01:09:47.218
Get back.


01:09:47.600 --> 01:09:49.663
Get back in. Get back in.


01:09:49.688 --> 01:09:51.956
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪


01:09:53.333 --> 01:09:54.644
Idiot!


01:09:57.777 --> 01:09:59.823
I heard he was a great detective.


01:10:00.428 --> 01:10:02.559
He was a suicidal maniac.


01:10:02.845 --> 01:10:04.683
They were going to
suspend him, anyway.


01:10:04.838 --> 01:10:06.465
They found stuff in his drawers.


01:10:06.613 --> 01:10:09.617
Items he'd stolen from
various crime scenes.


01:10:10.138 --> 01:10:11.803
Is this him?


01:10:15.472 --> 01:10:17.075
Where'd you get this?


01:10:17.100 --> 01:10:18.709
From a colleague.


01:10:20.012 --> 01:10:22.263
Yes, that's him.


01:10:24.208 --> 01:10:26.668
He had this cabin
up on the coast.


01:10:26.752 --> 01:10:29.171
He used to get up there
to get smashed.


01:10:29.255 --> 01:10:31.759
He was probably drunk
when he shot himself.


01:10:37.049 --> 01:10:38.763
They look like coffee beans.


01:10:39.555 --> 01:10:41.602
Maybe he was trying
to sober up after all.


01:10:44.892 --> 01:10:46.394
You didn't check?


01:10:46.479 --> 01:10:49.281
The cabin was locked
from the inside.


01:10:49.306 --> 01:10:51.653
And he looked like that
when they found him.


01:10:51.687 --> 01:10:54.066
There wasn't anything
<i>to</i> check.


01:10:57.160 --> 01:10:58.706
Did he have any family?


01:10:58.910 --> 01:11:01.413
Wife who left him a year
before he killed himself. Uh...


01:11:02.326 --> 01:11:03.985
I think there was a daughter.


01:11:05.537 --> 01:11:07.370
You know where is now?


01:11:07.395 --> 01:11:08.664
Not a clue.


01:11:10.304 --> 01:11:12.556
Is the cabin still there?


01:11:18.608 --> 01:11:21.821
<i>What are you doing to my
fucking gun, you idiot?</i>


01:12:08.435 --> 01:12:09.832
Where's Harry?


01:12:11.490 --> 01:12:12.728
In Bergen.


01:13:28.950 --> 01:13:31.180
- Hello?
- Mr. Hole?


01:13:31.264 --> 01:13:32.867
This is Harry Hole's phone.


01:13:32.892 --> 01:13:34.446
Can I speak to him?


01:13:35.518 --> 01:13:38.026
He's not here right now, but
I can take the message for him.


01:13:38.140 --> 01:13:41.401
<i>Right, okay. Uh, this is Rebecca,
NRS at Telenor.</i>


01:13:41.426 --> 01:13:44.577
We picked up a signal from
a missing person's phone.


01:13:44.602 --> 01:13:46.016
Case number MP2.


01:13:46.033 --> 01:13:49.293
Um, I don't have any files
in front of me. Um, who's that?


01:13:49.295 --> 01:13:52.345
I'll check...
Birte Becker.


01:13:54.838 --> 01:13:57.330
- Wha... is it transmitting now?
<i>- Yeah.</i>


01:13:57.355 --> 01:13:59.069
Just got it in minutes ago.


01:13:59.094 --> 01:14:01.005
Yeah, but, w-wait,
is it moving right now?


01:14:01.030 --> 01:14:01.911
<i>No.</i>


01:14:01.936 --> 01:14:03.539
I'll send you the coordinates.


01:14:03.564 --> 01:14:05.127
No, just, w-what's the address?


01:14:05.222 --> 01:14:10.428
Uh, Parkway 1, 0139 Oslo.


01:14:10.453 --> 01:14:11.985
You sure that's correct?


01:14:12.010 --> 01:14:14.469
<i>Yes, Parkway 1.</i>


01:14:18.996 --> 01:14:20.723
Hey, are you all right?


01:15:55.393 --> 01:15:57.393
<i>This is Birte Becker.
Please leave a message.</i>


01:17:21.107 --> 01:17:23.201
Wednesday, unless you...


01:17:23.226 --> 01:17:24.368
Yes?


01:17:28.167 --> 01:17:30.167
- In his own garage?
- Yeah.


01:17:53.740 --> 01:17:56.283
Ah, the great Harry Hole.


01:17:57.449 --> 01:17:59.108
How many bodies?


01:17:59.133 --> 01:18:01.304
Birte Becker and Ms. Dahl.


01:18:01.329 --> 01:18:02.543
Where's Katrine?


01:18:02.568 --> 01:18:03.627
Suspended.


01:18:03.629 --> 01:18:05.938
She got a call telling her
they traced the Becker phone


01:18:05.963 --> 01:18:07.891
and didn't think to tell anyone.


01:18:07.931 --> 01:18:10.074
I asked you where she was.


01:18:10.101 --> 01:18:11.923
That's not my problem right now.


01:18:12.679 --> 01:18:14.782
He shot himself straight on.


01:18:16.258 --> 01:18:17.874
How'd he do that with a shotgun?


01:18:17.899 --> 01:18:20.565
It's too long, you have to angle it.


01:18:21.155 --> 01:18:23.668
Pellet marks should be
up there somewhere.


01:18:23.670 --> 01:18:26.841
Luckily, we have experts
to determine that.


01:18:29.123 --> 01:18:30.782
You sure he was alone?


01:18:30.807 --> 01:18:33.789
The garage door was closed.
One set of footprints.


01:18:33.791 --> 01:18:37.579
We found two bodies in the house
and Birte Becker's phone.


01:18:39.390 --> 01:18:41.240
It was a suicide.


01:18:41.390 --> 01:18:43.104
Case closed.


01:18:49.150 --> 01:18:52.629
Mathias, listen,
I have no idea where he's gone.


01:18:54.266 --> 01:18:57.012
Yes, I've checked my messages,
he hasn't called.


01:18:57.329 --> 01:19:01.491
Oh, well, how can you help?
You're at your bloody conference!


01:19:03.091 --> 01:19:04.765
Can I keep this?


01:19:09.296 --> 01:19:10.947
Can I keep this?


01:19:13.398 --> 01:19:14.613
Yeah, sure.


01:19:21.087 --> 01:19:22.983
She's not picking up.


01:19:31.232 --> 01:19:33.010
Katrine!


01:19:53.492 --> 01:19:55.188
Get off me!


01:19:57.810 --> 01:19:59.193
Stop.


01:20:06.616 --> 01:20:09.552
I guess congratulations are in order.


01:20:09.983 --> 01:20:15.584
You know it wasn't that creep.
Vetlesen didn't commit suicide.


01:20:15.981 --> 01:20:19.385
Someone killed him because
we got too close.


01:20:26.765 --> 01:20:28.684
Like your father.


01:20:29.986 --> 01:20:32.661
My father would never have
committed suicide.


01:20:32.848 --> 01:20:35.398
He would never have
left me like that.


01:20:35.506 --> 01:20:36.681
Get off me.


01:20:36.713 --> 01:20:38.435
Get off me, get off me!


01:20:38.460 --> 01:20:39.641
Get off me!


01:20:39.689 --> 01:20:42.491
Get off me you fucking drunk!


01:20:42.570 --> 01:20:43.792
Get off.


01:20:44.474 --> 01:20:45.752
Get off.


01:20:46.233 --> 01:20:47.852
Yeah.


01:20:49.320 --> 01:20:51.137
I'm a drunk.


01:20:55.130 --> 01:20:57.221
Like your father.


01:21:13.716 --> 01:21:16.112
Laila Aasen and Arve Stop
were having an affair...


01:21:16.137 --> 01:21:19.827
and that's the last thing my father
was investigating before he got killed.


01:21:22.181 --> 01:21:24.094
You broke in to Vetlesen's house


01:21:24.119 --> 01:21:26.720
because you were afraid
I'd find out this was personal


01:21:26.745 --> 01:21:28.117
and take you off the case.


01:21:28.142 --> 01:21:29.815
Vetlesen was his pimp.


01:21:29.840 --> 01:21:32.133
And they were both in Bergen
when the murders started.


01:21:32.158 --> 01:21:35.869
I know how much you want this,
but you can't force the pieces to fit.


01:21:35.871 --> 01:21:39.158
I called the Gellion clinic
and Vetlesen wasn't even working


01:21:39.160 --> 01:21:41.442
the day he was supposed
to meet Birte Becker.


01:21:42.480 --> 01:21:45.773
They found two dead bodies in his
house and Birte Becker's phone.


01:21:45.775 --> 01:21:47.155
Isn't that convenient, then?


01:21:47.239 --> 01:21:49.696
So Hagen has his killer
and Arve Stop's safe.


01:21:49.721 --> 01:21:51.227
And no questions are asked.


01:21:52.078 --> 01:21:54.324
Do you actually think
he killed them?


01:21:54.460 --> 01:21:55.776
I don't know.


01:21:56.626 --> 01:21:59.193
I don't think either of us
do for sure.


01:22:05.597 --> 01:22:07.382
Maybe this will bring your balls back.


01:22:27.698 --> 01:22:29.888
I'm gonna need your weapon.


01:22:30.023 --> 01:22:32.198
It's right there
in front of you.


01:22:47.922 --> 01:22:50.213
Why did he call you Cloudberry?


01:22:54.931 --> 01:22:59.775
Because I liked
cloudberry jam with ice cream.


01:24:33.980 --> 01:24:36.151
Oleg ran away again.


01:24:52.919 --> 01:24:57.053
It doesn't really matter if
we win or lose this bid tonight.


01:24:57.549 --> 01:24:59.224
What matters most is that...


01:24:59.249 --> 01:25:01.466
we celebrate the way
this has brought us together.


01:25:01.930 --> 01:25:05.866
And use that energy to restore
the values that make Noway great.


01:25:06.267 --> 01:25:08.770
And so, it doesn't matter if uh...


01:25:08.855 --> 01:25:11.942
56 minutes and 33 seconds
from now, but who's counting...


01:25:13.846 --> 01:25:17.814
if the World Cup goes to
Beijing or Denver or Montreal.


01:25:18.827 --> 01:25:21.112
Because I believe in my heart...


01:25:21.184 --> 01:25:23.009
tonight...


01:25:23.351 --> 01:25:25.287
Oslo has already won.


01:25:29.423 --> 01:25:32.463
I tried calling.
I thought he might be with you.


01:25:33.854 --> 01:25:34.886
Oh.


01:25:34.911 --> 01:25:37.728
He's okay.
He's uh, he's at a friend's house.


01:25:38.767 --> 01:25:41.211
Just didn't bother calling me.


01:25:42.592 --> 01:25:44.409
What did you argue about?


01:25:46.092 --> 01:25:48.194
He doesn't want to leave the city.


01:25:49.696 --> 01:25:53.442
I thought that change
would be good for him.


01:25:54.124 --> 01:25:55.592
Well, for me too.


01:25:58.330 --> 01:25:59.719
Where?


01:25:59.744 --> 01:26:03.453
Um, Mathias has a house uh,
up in Telemark.


01:26:04.947 --> 01:26:07.645
And because he consults
all over the place...


01:26:08.264 --> 01:26:09.819
it's not too inconvenient.


01:26:10.765 --> 01:26:13.669
I saw him the other day,
he didn't mention anything.


01:26:17.437 --> 01:26:19.730
Is that really what you want?


01:26:21.257 --> 01:26:23.478
I don't know what I want.


01:26:29.828 --> 01:26:31.542
I miss you.


01:26:37.546 --> 01:26:41.263
<i>My head says 50/50,
but in my heart, 100%.</i>


01:26:41.288 --> 01:26:42.476
Thank you for coming.


01:26:42.501 --> 01:26:45.085
Mr. Stop?
Mr. Stop, I'm sorry, I um...


01:26:45.888 --> 01:26:47.721
I just want to thank you.


01:26:47.746 --> 01:26:50.253
I really liked your speech.


01:26:50.255 --> 01:26:53.108
I found it very... very moving.


01:26:54.398 --> 01:26:56.120
Well, you see, I uh...


01:26:57.247 --> 01:26:59.792
I was an orphan myself, so...


01:27:00.906 --> 01:27:04.746
Well, it doesn't have to be
a disadvantage, young lady.


01:27:05.066 --> 01:27:07.408
It can motivate us, too.


01:27:07.940 --> 01:27:08.876
Oh.


01:27:09.988 --> 01:27:11.377
Well, yes.


01:27:13.757 --> 01:27:17.757
I work in Bergen with-
with young people in a care center


01:27:17.782 --> 01:27:19.901
and I know how-
how very busy you are.


01:27:19.926 --> 01:27:21.423
But if ever you're
ever in the city...


01:27:21.448 --> 01:27:23.034
I started my career in Bergen.


01:27:24.771 --> 01:27:26.866
Write to me.
I'll see what I can do.


01:27:26.929 --> 01:27:28.517
Yes, I'm so sorry, I know...


01:27:28.542 --> 01:27:30.477
I know people are waiting
to talk to you. Thank you.


01:27:30.502 --> 01:27:32.320
- Not at all.
- Oh.


01:27:37.525 --> 01:27:38.684
Yes.


01:27:44.002 --> 01:27:47.740
Mr. Stop wanted me to let you know
how much he enjoyed your conversation.


01:27:47.765 --> 01:27:50.626
- Oh.
- It's um, it's room 472.


01:27:52.483 --> 01:27:54.522
He'll be free after
the announcement


01:27:54.547 --> 01:27:56.657
if there's anything else
you'd like to ask him.


01:27:56.784 --> 01:27:58.038
Thank you.


01:29:55.273 --> 01:29:56.681
Mathias.


01:29:56.991 --> 01:29:58.335
<i>Where are you?</i>


01:29:58.681 --> 01:30:00.779
I just tried calling you
on the landline.


01:30:02.354 --> 01:30:04.172
I'm at Harry's.


01:30:05.345 --> 01:30:06.481
<i>Yeah?</i>


01:30:06.911 --> 01:30:10.506
Because I phoned Eric's parents
and Oleg wasn't there either, so...


01:30:10.569 --> 01:30:11.855
<i>No, no. I found him.</i>


01:30:11.880 --> 01:30:14.185
He was with another friend.


01:30:17.855 --> 01:30:19.085
Are you okay?


01:30:19.110 --> 01:30:21.167
Yes, I-I'm fine now.


01:30:24.808 --> 01:30:26.252
Mathias...


01:30:26.277 --> 01:30:29.569
<i>Eh, I've got to run now to one
of those boring dinners, but...</i>


01:30:29.594 --> 01:30:33.118
I'll call you in the morning
when I'm back. Okay?


01:30:44.102 --> 01:30:45.499
Shit.


01:31:34.392 --> 01:31:37.151
You couldn't have asked
another doctor?


01:31:37.771 --> 01:31:38.937
What?


01:31:46.388 --> 01:31:48.441
<i>Two minutes,
ladies and gentlemen.</i>


01:32:25.601 --> 01:32:26.878
Hello?


01:32:28.974 --> 01:32:30.129
Hello?


01:32:37.376 --> 01:32:40.279
<i>And to all our viewers
around the world, thank you...</i>


01:32:44.637 --> 01:32:46.542
No. No!


01:32:46.567 --> 01:32:49.099
Stop. No!


01:32:49.129 --> 01:32:50.597
No!


01:32:51.810 --> 01:32:55.190
<i>Of Beijing, Denver, Oslo
and Montreal.</i>


01:32:55.274 --> 01:32:56.605
No!


01:33:01.397 --> 01:33:03.359
<i>There can only be one winner.</i>


01:33:09.951 --> 01:33:12.487
<i>The 15th Winter Sports
World Cup...</i>


01:33:12.582 --> 01:33:14.228
<i>has been awarded to...</i>


01:33:14.253 --> 01:33:15.863
Two, one...


01:33:16.046 --> 01:33:17.641
<i>Oslo.</i>


01:33:45.974 --> 01:33:49.410
Oslo! Oslo! Oslo!


01:33:51.995 --> 01:33:53.796
Congrats to us all.


01:34:08.959 --> 01:34:10.466
Hoo-hoo.


01:35:53.605 --> 01:35:55.970
That's the last
of her files to download.


01:35:56.279 --> 01:35:58.065
There's nothing after that.


01:36:00.041 --> 01:36:02.065
Get me a list of
all the phone calls


01:36:02.090 --> 01:36:04.105
and appointments she made
while I was away.


01:36:06.076 --> 01:36:07.457
Magnus!


01:36:10.362 --> 01:36:11.798
Yeah, sure.


01:36:15.658 --> 01:36:17.127
When was this taken?


01:36:17.317 --> 01:36:18.619
Two days ago.


01:36:18.621 --> 01:36:20.827
<i>- No, no. I'm late...
- I'm sorry, I'm sorry.</i>


01:36:20.852 --> 01:36:22.691
<i>to get her to school.
I have to get to work.</i>


01:36:22.716 --> 01:36:24.994
<i>I'm sorry. I have one quick
question I need to ask you.</i>


01:36:25.200 --> 01:36:26.858
<i>- We have been over this...
- I know.</i>


01:36:26.883 --> 01:36:27.811
<i>hundreds of times.</i>


01:36:27.858 --> 01:36:29.365
<i>I know we have been over this
a hundred times,</i>


01:36:29.390 --> 01:36:30.531
<i>but I need to sort something out.</i>


01:36:30.564 --> 01:36:33.190
<i>Dr. Vetlesen was not
working at the clinic</i>


01:36:33.215 --> 01:36:34.959
<i>the day your wife
was supposed to see him.</i>


01:36:34.961 --> 01:36:36.254
<i>He wasn't there..</i>


01:36:36.302 --> 01:36:38.647
<i>So she got the date wrong.</i>


01:36:38.672 --> 01:36:40.050
<i>- How...
- Daddy!</i>


01:36:40.134 --> 01:36:42.097
<i>Josephine, in the car.</i>


01:36:42.099 --> 01:36:45.716
<i>How the hell am I supposed to
remember what day we saw him?</i>


01:36:45.718 --> 01:36:48.448
<i>Sir, I'm just trying to find your wife.
Please help me.</i>


01:36:48.709 --> 01:36:52.135
<i>How the hell am I supposed to
remember what day we saw him?</i>


01:36:52.137 --> 01:36:55.477
<i>Sir, I'm just trying to find your wife.
Please help me.</i>


01:36:55.479 --> 01:36:57.792
<i>How the hell am I supposed to
remember what day we saw him?</i>


01:36:57.794 --> 01:36:59.658
<i>Sir, I'm just trying to find your wife.</i>


01:36:59.660 --> 01:37:01.892
<i>the hell am I supposed to
remember what day we saw him?</i>


01:37:01.917 --> 01:37:03.541
<i>Sir, I'm just trying to find your wife.</i>


01:37:03.566 --> 01:37:05.019
<i>- what day we saw him?
- Sir...</i>


01:37:05.044 --> 01:37:06.409
<i>- what day we saw him?
- Sir...</i>


01:37:07.475 --> 01:37:09.189
Yes, I want all those files.


01:37:09.237 --> 01:37:10.657
Give me your car keys.


01:37:10.689 --> 01:37:12.581
- What?
- And your phone.


01:37:43.843 --> 01:37:45.105
Yes?


01:37:47.448 --> 01:37:50.302
You told me Vetlesen was your
wife's doctor when we spoke.


01:37:51.368 --> 01:37:53.685
And that you had no idea
why she'd gone to see him.


01:37:54.233 --> 01:37:55.412
Yes.


01:37:57.416 --> 01:38:00.752
But you told my colleague
you both went to see him.


01:38:01.759 --> 01:38:03.735
She must have misheard me.


01:38:05.076 --> 01:38:06.909
She recorded the interview.


01:38:12.602 --> 01:38:15.096
Darling, go back inside.
I'll come in in a minute, okay?


01:38:18.084 --> 01:38:19.663
Good girl.


01:38:21.076 --> 01:38:22.587
She isn't mine.


01:38:25.133 --> 01:38:27.744
Birte and I were trying
for another child.


01:38:29.679 --> 01:38:31.910
We thought it might
save our marriage.


01:38:32.837 --> 01:38:36.061
We had blood tests done in the
clinic for hormone treatment.


01:38:36.769 --> 01:38:38.777
And it came out that...


01:38:39.991 --> 01:38:41.739
she wasn't mine.


01:38:44.412 --> 01:38:46.254
I am infertile.


01:38:46.523 --> 01:38:48.390
Always been infertile.


01:38:50.580 --> 01:38:52.263
Can't have children.


01:38:53.722 --> 01:38:55.428
But she is mine.


01:38:55.748 --> 01:38:57.573
Do you understand?


01:38:58.422 --> 01:39:00.295
How can I not love her?


01:39:04.013 --> 01:39:07.243
But you didn't see Vetlesen
the day you found out?


01:39:12.476 --> 01:39:15.874
No, we saw some
hormone specialist.


01:39:16.364 --> 01:39:18.468
Visiting consultant.


01:39:24.394 --> 01:39:26.402
Do you know his name?


01:39:34.742 --> 01:39:36.088
Yes?


01:39:39.296 --> 01:39:40.765
Just a second.


01:39:42.430 --> 01:39:43.613
Damn it.


01:39:45.839 --> 01:39:48.030
I said I'm coming.


01:39:54.973 --> 01:39:56.600
You never called.


01:39:58.381 --> 01:39:59.958
Is Oleg back?


01:40:00.350 --> 01:40:03.114
What? Oleg?
He-he's at school.


01:40:05.165 --> 01:40:07.078
And Harry?


01:40:07.887 --> 01:40:09.276
Is Harry here?


01:40:11.413 --> 01:40:12.746
No.


01:40:12.976 --> 01:40:14.024
No?


01:40:16.689 --> 01:40:20.029
How did he convince you
to give him those pills?


01:40:20.776 --> 01:40:22.126
He didn't.


01:40:24.006 --> 01:40:25.934
You didn't have to do it for me.


01:40:26.171 --> 01:40:27.918
I didn't do it for you.


01:40:38.067 --> 01:40:40.051
It was never about you.


01:40:53.462 --> 01:40:55.684
I'm outside his house.


01:40:55.709 --> 01:40:58.677
I can't reach Rakel.
Send someone to her apartment.


01:41:23.448 --> 01:41:24.535
Oleg.


01:41:24.765 --> 01:41:26.495
Sorry to keep you waiting.


01:41:46.807 --> 01:41:49.102
Why do you have Mom's phone?


01:41:53.048 --> 01:41:54.167
Come on.


01:42:09.868 --> 01:42:12.225
You and I have more
in common than you think.


01:42:15.280 --> 01:42:17.913
I didn't know who
my father was either.


01:42:36.080 --> 01:42:38.525
Magnus, track Rakel's phone.


01:42:49.412 --> 01:42:51.038
Sorry, I...


01:42:56.375 --> 01:42:57.628
All right.


01:42:59.264 --> 01:43:01.534
Okay, Harry, we just
picked up a signal.


01:43:01.559 --> 01:43:03.233
Heading west towards Telemark.


01:43:03.258 --> 01:43:07.960
It is a red Volvo, registered to a
Mathias Lund-Helgesen...


01:43:07.962 --> 01:43:09.973
Rjukan, 2421.


01:43:12.302 --> 01:43:13.853
<i>The house is pretty remote.</i>


01:43:13.855 --> 01:43:15.990
There-there's an access
road, but that's it.


01:43:16.015 --> 01:43:17.659
And there's a big lake around it.


01:43:18.511 --> 01:43:20.519
Helicopters are grounded
because of the weather.


01:43:20.544 --> 01:43:21.994
But Delta is on their way.


01:43:24.779 --> 01:43:26.874
Anything on Mathias' family?


01:43:26.899 --> 01:43:28.191
<i>Okay, I've got something here.</i>


01:43:28.193 --> 01:43:32.702
Jonas Lund-Helgesen, former
police officer, lost his job in '89.


01:43:33.120 --> 01:43:36.459
A scandal involving
a woman drowning in a car.


01:43:36.539 --> 01:43:37.928
Probable suicide.


01:43:37.953 --> 01:43:40.023
<i>She had a son.</i>


01:43:40.048 --> 01:43:40.794
Stop!


01:43:40.880 --> 01:43:42.546
<i>Father, unknown.</i>


01:43:42.571 --> 01:43:43.519
Please!


01:43:43.521 --> 01:43:45.592
<i>He was sent to an orphanage.</i>


01:43:53.462 --> 01:43:55.970
Who led the investigation
into the woman's disappearance?


01:43:56.643 --> 01:43:59.354
<i>Some local talent in village nearby.</i>


01:43:59.438 --> 01:44:00.692
<i>What's his name?</i>


01:44:00.717 --> 01:44:02.857
Jonas Lund-Helgesen.


01:44:03.858 --> 01:44:07.666
Jonas. No.
Please, stop!


01:44:27.723 --> 01:44:28.771
Harry?


01:44:29.152 --> 01:44:30.256
Harry!


01:44:30.295 --> 01:44:31.645
We've lost him.


01:46:29.212 --> 01:46:31.214
Sit down, Harry.


01:46:42.517 --> 01:46:43.894
Pass me the gun.


01:46:53.904 --> 01:46:55.990
I didn't think you'd find me.


01:46:58.410 --> 01:47:01.508
Perhaps the pills helped after all.


01:47:03.666 --> 01:47:06.333
I spoke to Filip Becker.


01:47:09.326 --> 01:47:11.072
What's going to happen


01:47:11.097 --> 01:47:14.318
when Josephine Becker finds out
he isn't her father?


01:47:16.711 --> 01:47:18.633
She'll still love him.


01:47:18.886 --> 01:47:20.178
Wrong answer.


01:47:30.729 --> 01:47:32.094
Let's try again.


01:47:34.184 --> 01:47:38.046
Was it right for Sylvia Ottersen
to kill her unborn child...


01:47:38.525 --> 01:47:42.037
simply because she couldn't
keep track of who the father was?


01:47:44.447 --> 01:47:46.603
That was her choice.


01:47:49.236 --> 01:47:50.776
Too short.


01:47:51.062 --> 01:47:52.808
Maybe she was afraid.


01:47:56.627 --> 01:47:58.793
What about you, Harry?


01:48:00.423 --> 01:48:02.550
You have a woman who loves you.


01:48:03.438 --> 01:48:05.362
A boy who's devoted to you.


01:48:06.929 --> 01:48:09.068
Why did you abandon them?


01:48:11.715 --> 01:48:13.588
They deserve better.


01:48:16.040 --> 01:48:17.356
Too easy.


01:48:18.565 --> 01:48:21.280
Because I'm selfish.


01:48:24.608 --> 01:48:26.258
I'm an addict.


01:48:29.368 --> 01:48:32.026
There isn't enough room for them.


01:48:48.343 --> 01:48:51.846
You know, when I first saw
your picture in the papers...


01:48:53.516 --> 01:48:55.540
with all those medals...


01:48:57.019 --> 01:49:01.622
I thought, "That man
must have a perfect family."


01:49:07.130 --> 01:49:08.829
And here you are.


01:49:11.154 --> 01:49:13.013
Last question.


01:49:13.884 --> 01:49:15.479
This boy...


01:49:16.304 --> 01:49:18.694
who doesn't even know
who his father is...


01:49:19.975 --> 01:49:22.959
who's had to put up with
so many men like you and me...


01:49:22.984 --> 01:49:24.762
taking his place.


01:49:28.775 --> 01:49:31.311
Does his mother deserve to live?


01:49:35.366 --> 01:49:38.241
Why don't you ask him?


01:50:22.245 --> 01:50:23.914
You all right?


01:50:27.290 --> 01:50:28.488
Kill him.


01:50:29.083 --> 01:50:30.193
Kill him.


01:50:31.214 --> 01:50:32.503
Kill him!


01:51:08.991 --> 01:51:10.418
Come on!


01:51:11.750 --> 01:51:13.290
I'm ready!


01:51:14.457 --> 01:51:15.941
I'm here!


01:51:16.473 --> 01:51:18.119
Come on!


01:51:50.365 --> 01:51:52.575
I know why you blame her.


01:52:02.194 --> 01:52:05.796
You've been wrong
the whole time.


01:52:11.992 --> 01:52:13.730
It wasn't her.


01:52:19.714 --> 01:52:22.412
It wasn't you mother
who didn't want you.


01:52:25.151 --> 01:52:26.960
<i>It was your father.</i>


01:52:30.405 --> 01:52:33.199
It would have been better for him...


01:52:36.371 --> 01:52:38.120
had you not been born.


01:54:00.747 --> 01:54:04.260
The pathologist detected traces
of the drug ketanome.


01:54:04.415 --> 01:54:06.523
And the direct cause of death
was drowning...


01:54:06.548 --> 01:54:08.474
as the result of blood
filling her lungs.


01:54:08.919 --> 01:54:11.404
24 stab wounds were found
in her mouth...


01:54:11.758 --> 01:54:13.468
all at regular intervals...


01:54:13.552 --> 01:54:15.758
and at the same depth:
seven centimeters.


01:54:16.281 --> 01:54:19.068
The pathologist can't determine
what kind of weapon was used.


01:54:19.688 --> 01:54:21.648
And he's never seen
anything like it.


01:54:22.933 --> 01:54:25.028
I'll take it.


01:54:27.240 --> 01:54:29.248
Subs by enwansix
@ subs4free.info
